    <node id="&quot;GREENHOUSE GAS EMISSIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1"> Greenhouse Gas Emissions are substances that trap heat in the atmosphere, contributing significantly to climate change. These emissions are under scrutiny not only for their impact on global warming but also in relation to crop residue removal. The study of Greenhouse Gas Emissions in this context aims to understand how the process of removing crop residues influences the overall emission levels and potentially offers insights into sustainable agricultural practices.</data>
      <data key="d2">07110d5763e07d0f5f4dd938ec1ba1bc,1bb1770e8d4b92e8827eea5f67912f09,62be9ce3d6b8bf802c766aa56811e0f1</data>
