    <node id="&quot;FAO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1"> The Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO) is an international organization that primarily conducts research. Its areas of focus include investigating the effects of biochar, irrigation, drought, and various agricultural practices on crop productivity and greenhouse gas emissions. Specifically, it studies topics such as microbial biomass carbon and soil moisture. Additionally, the FAO provides information about nitrous oxide emissions, net global warming potential, and rice yields in Southeast Asia. Currently, the FAO is engaged in a study examining the impact of removing crop residues like corn stover and wheat straw on crop productivity, soil health, and greenhouse gas emissions.</data>
      <data key="d2">1bb1770e8d4b92e8827eea5f67912f09,3327c11d57a6c03e04644a96164ceb62,3a22b4bc263900ce77dd6b34cf949ed2,8f13ed1b9204eca24d5bb01b87dd4fd4,f11dee47362dfe1c5da0ee97f088b7f3</data>
