      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1"> Ocean Acidification, conceptually referred to as a decrease in the pH level of the ocean, is primarily caused by increased carbon dioxide emissions. This phenomenon affects marine life and ecosystems significantly, altering their chemical balance and potentially threatening various species' survival.</data>
