    <node id="&quot;SOIL CARBON STOCKS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1"> Soil Carbon Stocks are the total quantity of carbon that is stored within the soil. This storage plays a crucial role in maintaining soil fertility and serves as an essential element in mitigating climate change. The carbon stored in the soil helps to maintain soil health, improve productivity, and sequester atmospheric carbon dioxide, thereby reducing greenhouse gas emissions and contributing to global efforts against climate change.</data>
