    <node id="&quot;EVENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1"> The EVENT under discussion revolves around two interconnected topics. Initially, it is revealed as a discourse concerning nitrous oxide. However, upon further examination, it transpires that this EVENT is essentially a research project. This research focuses on the exploration of the effects of substituting organic fertilizers for mineral fertilizers in maize cultivation. The primary objectives of this research include assessing the impact on maize yields, nitrogen use efficiency, nitrogen losses, carbon emissions, and the rate of soil organic carbon sequestration. Thus, the EVENT encompasses a comprehensive study of the agricultural implications and environmental consequences of such a substitution.</data>
      <data key="d2">8e40b801b28308601a12691f8bf2b7ca,e365e08ecc6f471b0ce073a8c60482e1</data>
      <data key="d3">6</data>
      <data key="d4">134</data>
      <data key="d5">cd130938a2844050be991af70baf5ee0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORGANIZATION/PERSON&quot;">
